# Query objects

- Naming de métodos/variáveis → `naming-rails.mdc`. Nome de classe = **pedido de leitura** + sufixo `Query`.
- **When:** non-trivial / reused AR composition (filters, joins, order, counts, small read-only aggregations as `Hash`). **Else:** one-liner filter → model scope; mutação de objetos → use case (`use_cases.mdc`); pergunta de domínio (`esta`/`tem`/`possui`/`pode`) → rule object (`rule_objects.mdc`).
- **Name (obrigatório):** ao escrever o identificador, use uma referência de pedido: **`obter`**, **`identificar`**, **`montar`**, **`capturar`**, **`contar`**, **`calcular`**. Sempre sufixo `Query`. Ex.: `ObterPedidosRecentesQuery`, `ContarIngressosVendidosQuery`, `CalcularTotalDoPedidoQuery` — **não** `PedidosRecentesQuery` (falta o pedido), **não** `QuaisPedidosRecentesQuery` (pergunta = rule), **não** `CriarPedidosQuery` (mutação = use case). **NS:** `DominioX::Queries::Y::`. **Path:** `app/domains/<domain>/queries/**/name_query.rb` ↔ nested `Y::`.
- **Doc:** class comment pode descrever a intenção em pt-BR; o identificador nomeia o **pedido** (verbo da tabela) + o alvo.

## Invariants

- **API:** `def self.call(...) = new(...).call` — public entry **only** at class level through `self.call` (same pattern as `new(...).call`).
- **Return:** `ActiveRecord::Relation<Model>` **or** `Hash` (aggregations). Caller owns pagination, `find`, iteration — query returns relation/hash only.
- **Read-only:** no writes, callbacks, jobs, mail, side effects (no `each(&:touch)` etc.).
- **Input:** validated kwargs — **never** raw `params`. Normalize variants in `initialize` (e.g. `id:` vs `ids:` → one internal shape).
- **Base relation:** starting relation kwarg **must** be named `relation:`; store as `@relation`; thread `relation:` through `self.call` defaulting to `Model.all` when applicable.
- **Includes:** prefer `preload` when associations are for display/preload only and no `where`/`order` on joined tables; use `includes` only when needed for conditional SQL on associations.
- **Reuse:** prefer existing model **named scopes** over duplicating `where` strings.
- **Structure:** `#call` pode conter a composição quando for curta e linear; decompose em privados quando as cláusulas crescerem ou se misturarem.
- **Perf:** never `SomeQuery.new` / `.call` **inside** a loop — build relation once, then iterate.
- **YARD (mandatory):** both `self.call` and `#call` need `# @return [ActiveRecord::Relation<Model>]` or `# @return [Hash]` (narrow `Hash{...}` when useful) — same bar as rule objects’ non-boolean `#result`.

## Do not

- Mutations or touching records; pagination inside query object; raw `params`; kwarg named `scope:` / `base_query:` instead of `relation:`; ivar named other than `@relation` for the base; returning non-relation/non-hash domain objects; instantiating query per row in a loop; nomes em inglês (`RecentOrdersQuery`, `GetOrdersQuery`); nomes sem pedido (`PedidosRecentesQuery`); interrogativos (`Quais…`, `Esta…`, `Pode…Query`) — isso é rule; verbos de mutação (`Criar…Query`).

## Reference skeleton

```ruby
# Obter pedidos recentes (opcionalmente filtrados por status).
module DominioOrders
  module Queries
    module Orders
      class ObterPedidosRecentesQuery
        # @return [ActiveRecord::Relation<Order>]
        def self.call(status: nil, relation: Order.all)
          new(status:, relation:).call
        end

        def initialize(status: nil, relation: Order.all)
          @status = status
          @relation = relation
        end

        # @return [ActiveRecord::Relation<Order>]
        def call
          orders = @relation.preload(:customer).where("created_at > ?", 30.days.ago)
          @status ? orders.where(status: @status) : orders
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
```
